ory="XE" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-4835524-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>4835524</doc-number> <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5866891-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country> <doc-number>5866891</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1045526A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI MATERIALS CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UOZUMI GAKUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI MATERIALS CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UOZUMI, GAKUJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UOZUMI GAKUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UOZUMI, GAKUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A number of tags are identified individually even if they overlap one another or overlap a metal plate. Tags (11-13) attached to an article have an antenna coil (14) and a RFID element (16) connected to the antenna coil (14). The antenna coil (14) and the RFID element (16) form a resonant circuit (24), which is provided with a normally closed switch (26) capable for opening the resonant circuit (24). The switch (26) is connected with a time constant circuit (27) that operates the switch (26) at predetermined time intervals while current flows in the resonant circuit (24). The time constant circuit (27) opens the switch (26) for different periods of time for different tags (11-13).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon l'invention, on identifie individuellement un certain nombre d'étiquettes, même si celles-ci se chevauchent ou chevauchent une plaque métallique. Des étiquettes (11-13) fixées sur un article possèdent une bobine d'antenne (14), ainsi qu'un élément d'identification de fréquence radio (RFID) (16) connecté à la bobine (14), laquelle avec cet élément RFID (16) forme un circuit oscillant (24), doté d'un commutateur normalement fermé (26), capable d'ouvrir ce circuit oscillant (24). Le commutateur (26) est connecté à un montage à constante de temps (27) commandant le commutateur (26) à des intervalles de temps déterminés pendant que le courant circule dans le circuit oscillant (24). Le montage à constante de temps (27) ouvre le commutateur (26) pendant des périodes de temps différentes destinées à des étiquettes différentes (11-13).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>